+    },
+    {
+      "key": "raw-bridge",
+      "namespace": "probability.percolation",
+      "logical_name": "raw-axial-monotone-fpp-transfer-hypothesis",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Draft audit target: raw axial monotone FPP transfer",
+      "statement": "DRAFT AUXILIARY HYPOTHESIS FOR AUDIT, NOT A THEOREM: For a fixed iid finite nonnegative nonconstant edge law on nearest-neighbor Z^2, could the unrestricted value T_N and the monotone axial value D_N satisfy D_N-T_N=o(N) almost surely? Narrow bounded support alone does not validate this route; the independently checked detour derivation gives a positive lower linear gap. This question concerns the uncentered axial restriction and does not assert a bridge for differently centered fluctuations or interior directions.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": [
+        "one fixed iid finite nonnegative nonconstant edge law",
+        "raw axial passage values as defined in axial-values"
+      ],
+      "domain": "probability",
+      "source": {
+        "source_id": "owner:probability300:P0110:w379:raw-bridge",
+        "url": "file:///~/brain_workers/w379/INDEPENDENT.md",
+        "revision": "2026-10-10-w380-keep-draft",
+        "license": "owner-own-work",
+        "excerpt": null
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "key": "finite-detour",
+      "namespace": "probability.percolation",
+      "logical_name": "finite-axial-detour-obstruction-to-monotone-restriction",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Reviewed draft: finite axial detour obstruction",
+      "statement": "DRAFT MATHEMATICAL DERIVATION, INDEPENDENTLY CHECKED BY w380 (KEEP); COORDINATOR INTEGRATION PENDING: For iid finite nonnegative nonconstant edge weights on Z^2, choose 0<l<h with p_l=P(tau<=l)>0 and p_h=P(tau>=h)>0 and integer n>2l/(h-l). The n-edge direct axis path and a height-one detour of n+2 edges share no edges. The event that all direct edges are >=h and all detour edges are <=l has probability q=p_h^n p_l^(n+2)>0 and yields D_n-T_n>=delta=n(h-l)-2l>0. For fair weights {1,2} take n=3: the direct cost is 6, a detour costs 5, and this event has probability 1/256. No values on other edges are imposed.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": [
+        "iid finite nonnegative nonconstant edge law",
+        "l,h,n,p_l,p_h as stated"
+      ],
+      "domain": "probability",
+      "source": {
+        "source_id": "owner:probability300:P0110:w379:finite-detour",
+        "url": "file:///~/brain_workers/w379/INDEPENDENT.md",
+        "revision": "2026-10-10-w380-keep-draft",
+        "license": "owner-own-work",
+        "excerpt": null
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "key": "linear-gap",
+      "namespace": "probability.percolation",
+      "logical_name": "positive-linear-axial-monotone-restriction-gap",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Reviewed draft: positive linear axial restriction gap",
+      "statement": "DRAFT MATHEMATICAL DERIVATION, INDEPENDENTLY CHECKED BY w380 (KEEP); COORDINATOR INTEGRATION PENDING: In iid FPP with finite nonnegative nonconstant weights on nearest-neighbor Z^2, let T_N be unrestricted passage from 0 to N e1 and D_N the unique monotone axial path sum. Choose 0<l<h with p_l=P(tau<=l)>0, p_h=P(tau>=h)>0, n>2l/(h-l), L=n+2, delta=n(h-l)-2l and q=p_h^n p_l^(n+2). Then almost surely liminf_{N->infinity}(D_N-T_N)/N>=delta*q/L>0. Independent detour blocks at spacing L give an explicit path saving delta for each successful block. If E tau=m<infinity, also limsup T_N/N<=m-delta*q/L. For fair {1,2} weights, n=3 gives the bound 1/1280. This is an independently checked special-case obstruction to raw axial transfer; it does not prove or refute the original existential KPZ exponent problem.",
